  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "The three-digit number \\(2a3\\) is added to the number \\(326\\) to give the three-digit number \\(5b9.\\) If \\(5b9\\) is divisible by \\(9,\\) then \\(a+b\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(6\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(8\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(9\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "6"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1967-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Divisibility by \\(9\\) requires \\(5+b+9\\) to be a multiple of \\(9.\\) Since \\(b\\) is a digit, this gives \\(b=4.\\) The addition is then \\(2a3+326=549,\\) so \\(a=2.\\) Hence \\(a+b=6.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the digit sum of \\(5b9\\)",
        "After finding \\(b,\\) compare the tens digits in the addition"
      ],
